  "body": "## #931 slice 3 of 3: the Setups combo lists the post's offsets; MCP takes an index\n\n**Stacked on #1113 → #1101** (#945, the former bottom of the stack, merged 2026-11-12). This PR targets `main`, so until those merge its diff also shows their commits. This slice is its own `feat(ui,mcp): ...` and `fix(ui): ...` commits. Merge order: #1101, #1113, then this one. Fork synced at v0.19.0.\n\n**Process change: yes** (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, the `set_work_offset` row). By the current process rule this PR does not edit `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` (it carries main's); the merging session handles the number and the #681 note.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\n### What changed\n- **Setups page / WCS page combo** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_wcs_pick.rs`): lists offsets `1..=max` of the setup's **own** post (`setup::work_offset_names`, the cached table from slice 2). Each entry reads \"Work offset n (NAME)\", or \"Work offset n\" when the post gives that offset no name. The default post shows 6 entries. Tormach PathPilot shows 9 (G59.1-G59.3). If a setup holds a pick its post cannot express, for example offset 9 after switching to a six-offset post, that pick still shows as itself: \"Work offset 9 - not on this post\", listed alone after 1-6. It is never shown as offset 1. The post gate from slice 2 refuses it by setup name.\n- **The wording is one function in app**: `setup_offsets::entry_label`.\n- **Other UI words.** Slice 2 already moved the browser tree, the heights row, the viewport chips and the status line to the app's names. This slice changes the three texts that still named a fixed \"G54-G59\" range: the combo's hover, the heights page hint, and the WCS page's \"Work offset:\" line. The WCS page line appears in a release-lane snapshot, which gets regenerated at the cut; its structural twin `one_wcs` is updated here. I left the probe page's \"Set G54\"..\"Set G59\" alone on purpose: the probe register arithmetic only reaches offsets 1-6 (triage point 4).\n- **MCP `set_work_offset`** (`crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs`):\n  - It takes `index`, 1-based. The words `G54`-`G59` are accepted as aliases of 1-6.\n  - `word` stays as the older spelling of the same argument. If both are given they must agree.\n  - `setup_offsets::parse_index` checks only the shape and the 1-255 sanity bound. The post's range is checked by `SetSetupWorkOffset::new` → `setup_offsets::check`, so the refusal is the same one the GUI gives, by setup name.\n  - Replies carry `index`, `name` and `word` (an alias of `name`). So do `set_wcs` and `get_job`'s `setups[].wcs` (`mcp/job.rs`).\n- **camcraft-mcp skill doc**: documents the new `set_work_offset` arguments and replies.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/931-wcs-index-ui.md`.\n\n### How it was tested\n- New: `crates/app/tests/mcp_work_offset.rs` (4 tests):\n  - `set_work_offset_takes_a_one_based_index_and_answers_index_name_and_word`\n  - `the_legacy_words_are_aliases_of_offsets_one_to_six`\n  - `an_offset_the_setups_post_cannot_express_is_refused_by_setup_name`\n  - `the_schema_offers_index_and_keeps_word`\n- New tests in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_wcs_tests.rs`. These are AccessKit assertions with the popup open:\n  - `the_combo_lists_the_setups_post_range_by_its_names`: 6 entries on the default post, 9 on Tormach\n  - `a_pick_beyond_the_post_stays_visible_and_says_so`\n- Updated: `an_unset_setup_reads_work_offset_one`, `the_picker_sets_the_setups_work_offset_through_the_command`, `offset_hint_names_the_real_pages_in_plain_words`, and the structural twin `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure` (asserts the combo value is \"Work offset 1 (G54)\" and no bare word).\n- **Refresh 9720520e** (refreshed #1113 @ 2871b646 merged, then upstream/main 7bfb1824): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green - post, app and ui suites, 3872 passed, 0 failed (26.9 min wall); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. The refresh changes no post script or stream logic beyond main's own commits.\n- Green: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (on de5829e8: post, app, ui suites, 0 failed); `mcp`, `mcp_setup`, `mcp_work_offset` and `wcs_index`; the ui lib, run from `crates/ui` (533 passed on the final head, `one_wcs` included); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n### Not exercised\n- GUI hand check: **done, passed** (the user, macOS arm64 release build of d97157c2, 2026-11-12).\n- **Hub run: PASS** (2026-11-13, the user): posted from d97157c2 with the Tormach PathPilot post on the 770MX sim (PathPilot v2.14.4), five setups at G54, G59, G59.1, G59.2, G59.3: no unknown-word error, G59.1/G59.3 shown active, all five cut, M30. G54/G59 byte-identical to main's; offset 10 refused by name.\n- The MCP refusal is pinned against the default 6-offset post only (main has since added `set_setup_post`; a Tormach-range MCP test through it is not added here). The Tormach range is pinned in app (`wcs_index`) and in the UI test.\n\nChangelog: Work offsets are picked by number, up to what the setup's own post supports. The Setups page lists them as \"Work offset n (NAME)\", so Tormach shows 9. MCP `set_work_offset` takes a 1-based `index`; G54-G59 still work as aliases, and replies add `index` and `name`. (#931)\n\nFixes #931\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
